## What is an Activation Error?

The **Activation Error** status appears when there is a problem activating one or more items on an order.  
This status ensures you are aware of an issue that requires your attention before the order can be fully activated.

## Why is the Activation Error status important?

It helps you quickly identify orders that need review or correction, preventing delays in delivering products or services to your customers.

## How to Resolve an Activation Error

1. **Open the order** that has the **Activation Error** status.
2. Look at the **Fulfilment** card in the order.
   - A red badge will appear next to any affected item.
   - Hover over the badge to see more details about the error.
3. For additional information:
   - Go to the **Account Group**.
   - Review the rejection reason in the **Products** card.
4. If applicable:
   - Select `Edit and resubmit` from the menu (kebab icon) on the rejected line item,  
     **OR**
   - Dismiss the error, resolve the underlying issue, and submit a new order for processing.
5. After submitting a corrected order:
   - Once retail subscriptions are reviewed, return to the order with the Activation Error.
   - Select the kebab menu in the top corner.
   - Choose `Ignore All Errors` to update the status to **Activated**.

Note:
Ignoring errors should only be done once you have reviewed and resolved any issues that could affect product delivery. Once the error is ignored the order will go back to its currnet status.

## Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs)

<details>
<summary>Will Activation Error stop my entire order from activating?</summary>

It may affect only the specific items with errors, but the order will remain in **Activation Error** status until resolved or ignored.
</details>

<details>
<summary>Can I fix only one item and leave others in error?</summary>

Yes. You can edit and resubmit individual line items in the account details page, and choose to ignore only all errors or specific errors on the order after reviewing them.
</details>

<details>
<summary>Where can I find the error details?</summary>

Details appear in the **Fulfilment** card (red badge tooltip) and in the **Products** card of the Account details.
</details>

<details>
<summary>When should I use “Ignore All Errors”?</summary>

Use it only after confirming that the remaining issues will not impact your customer’s services.
</details>

<details>
<summary>Can I prevent Activation Errors?</summary>

Most errors occur due to missing information, incorrect form entries, or account setup issues. Reviewing all order details before submission can help prevent them.
</details>

